Linaro xen-vhost-frontend a1e333c5: tear a device down even when its backend's reset or
shutdown panics, and do not let one panicked device thread poison every later one.
Applied after xen-vhost-frontend-a1e333c5.patch.

- XenDevice::exit(): reset() and shutdown() each run under catch_unwind (and a lock that a
  panic poisoned is taken back), so destroy_ioreq() always runs. Before, a panic in reset()
  skipped it and the guest's ioreq server and foreign mappings stayed.
- XenFrontend::add_device / remove_device: the FrontendGuests lock is taken with
  PoisonError::into_inner. Before, one panic with the lock held made every later add and
  remove panic with PoisonError, until the daemon was restarted.

Not in this patch (issue B): the add_device(...).unwrap() in main.rs, which panics with
XBInvalidState on the Raspberry Pi. It stays as it is so that the next bench run can show
whether it still appears.

Upstream: not opened (draft in xaloqi-knowledge campaigns/2026-11-10-xvf-teardown-issue-draft.md,
issue A); target vireshk/xen-vhost-frontend. Pairs with vireshk-vhost-abf24853-reset.patch.

diff --git a/src/device.rs b/src/device.rs
index fc76d96..4b85252 100644
--- a/src/device.rs
+++ b/src/device.rs
@@ -7,7 +7,8 @@ use clap::Parser;
 use seccompiler::SeccompAction;
 use std::{
     collections::HashMap,
-    sync::{Arc, Mutex},
+    panic::{catch_unwind, AssertUnwindSafe},
+    sync::{Arc, Mutex, PoisonError},
 };
 
 use lazy_static::lazy_static;
@@ -163,8 +164,19 @@ impl XenDevice {
             interrupt.exit();
         }
 
-        self.gdev.lock().unwrap().reset();
-        self.gdev.lock().unwrap().shutdown();
+        // The ioreq range must be released even if the backend's reset or shutdown panics,
+        // or the guest's foreign mappings and ioreq server stay and its domain cannot die.
+        let gdev = || self.gdev.lock().unwrap_or_else(PoisonError::into_inner);
+        if catch_unwind(AssertUnwindSafe(|| {
+            gdev().reset();
+        }))
+        .is_err()
+        {
+            log::error!("device {}: reset panicked, continuing the teardown", self.dev_id);
+        }
+        if catch_unwind(AssertUnwindSafe(|| gdev().shutdown())).is_err() {
+            log::error!("device {}: shutdown panicked, continuing the teardown", self.dev_id);
+        }
 
         self.destroy_ioreq().ok();
     }
